# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plugging into ffsim’s simulation interface {#plugging-into-ffsims-simulation-interface}"
msgstr "Terhubung ke antarmuka simulasi ffsim {#plugging-into-ffsims-simulation-interface}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) is a high-performance simulator for fermionic quantum circuits that exploits particle number and spin-Z conservation to represent state vectors more compactly than a generic $2^n$-dimensional qubit statevector. It defines protocols that any object can implement to participate in its simulation machinery (see [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") for this package’s own protocols, which follow the same design):\n"
msgstr "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) adalah simulator berkinerja tinggi untuk circuit kuantum fermionik yang memanfaatkan kekekalan jumlah partikel dan spin-Z untuk merepresentasikan state vector lebih ringkas daripada statevector qubit generik berdimensi $2^n$. ffsim mendefinisikan protokol yang bisa diimplementasikan objek apa pun agar ikut serta dalam mesin simulasinya (lihat [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") untuk protokol milik paket ini sendiri, yang mengikuti desain yang sama):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary.html#ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary \"(in ffsim)\"), by the method `_apply_unitary_(vec, norb, nelec, copy)`, applying the object as a unitary to a fixed-particle-number state vector\n"
msgstr "[`ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary.html#ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary \"(in ffsim)\"), lewat metode `_apply_unitary_(vec, norb, nelec, copy)`, yang menerapkan objek sebagai uniter ke state vector dengan jumlah partikel tetap\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), by the method `_linear_operator_(norb, nelec)`, returning a [`scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") view of the object on that same sector\n"
msgstr "[`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), lewat metode `_linear_operator_(norb, nelec)`, yang mengembalikan tampilan [`scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") dari objek pada sektor yang sama\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\"), by the method `_trace_(norb, nelec)`, returning the object’s trace on that sector.\n"
msgstr "[`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\"), lewat metode `_trace_(norb, nelec)`, yang mengembalikan trace objek pada sektor itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package implements that interface: every fermionic gate in [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") provides `_apply_unitary_`, and [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") provides `_linear_operator_` and `_trace_`. That is what makes this package’s operators and circuits *compatible* with ffsim, so its tools work on them natively, with no conversion step. [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") can simulate a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") end to end, [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\") can diagonalize a [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\"), and sampling utilities like [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") (used in the [SKQD guide](skqd#skqd-getting-started) to turn a simulated statevector into measurement counts) work without modification.\n"
msgstr "Paket ini mengimplementasikan antarmuka tersebut: setiap gate fermionik di [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") menyediakan `_apply_unitary_`, dan [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") menyediakan `_linear_operator_` dan `_trace_`. Itulah yang membuat operator dan circuit paket ini *kompatibel* dengan ffsim, sehingga perangkatnya bekerja secara native pada keduanya, tanpa langkah konversi. [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") bisa mensimulasikan [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") dari ujung ke ujung, [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\") bisa mendiagonalisasi [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\"), dan utilitas sampling seperti [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") (dipakai di [panduan SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) untuk mengubah statevector hasil simulasi menjadi counts pengukuran) bekerja tanpa modifikasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What `_linear_operator_` returns is an ordinary SciPy [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\"), so [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") and friends work on it too.\n"
msgstr "Yang dikembalikan `_linear_operator_` adalah [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") SciPy biasa, jadi [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") dan fungsi sejenis juga bisa dipakai padanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Coupling through ffsim’s protocols is what buys this: its actively developed ecosystem of simulation and sampling utilities applies to this package’s circuits and operators unchanged, and users already working with ffsim can mix in this package’s gates and operators without learning another simulation API.\n"
msgstr "Keuntungan dari penggabungan lewat protokol ffsim adalah ini: ekosistem utilitas simulasi dan sampling-nya yang aktif dikembangkan berlaku untuk circuit dan operator paket ini tanpa perubahan, dan pengguna yang sudah memakai ffsim bisa mencampurkan gate dan operator paket ini tanpa perlu mempelajari API simulasi lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "ffsim is an optional dependency {#ffsim-is-an-optional-dependency}"
msgstr "ffsim adalah dependensi opsional {#ffsim-is-an-optional-dependency}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ffsim is declared as an optional extra (`pip install \"qiskit-fermions[ffsim]\"`, or transitively by `[all]`), guarded at runtime by [`HAS_FFSIM`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/utils-optionals#qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM \"qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM\") (as was shown above). Installing it unlocks simulation: [`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\") and [`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\") are implemented by converting this package’s [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") into an [`ffsim.FermionOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.FermionOperator.html#ffsim.FermionOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), so without ffsim they raise [`MissingOptionalLibraryError`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/exceptions#qiskit.exceptions.MissingOptionalLibraryError). Everything that does not simulate (building operators, mapping them, and transpiling the resulting circuits) needs none of it.\n"
msgstr "ffsim dideklarasikan sebagai extra opsional (`pip install \"qiskit-fermions[ffsim]\"`, atau secara transitif lewat `[all]`), dijaga saat runtime oleh [`HAS_FFSIM`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/utils-optionals#qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM \"qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM\") (seperti yang ditunjukkan di atas). Memasangnya membuka kemampuan simulasi: [`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\") dan [`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\") diimplementasikan dengan mengonversi [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") milik paket ini menjadi [`ffsim.FermionOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.FermionOperator.html#ffsim.FermionOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), sehingga tanpa ffsim keduanya memunculkan [`MissingOptionalLibraryError`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/exceptions#qiskit.exceptions.MissingOptionalLibraryError). Semua yang tidak melakukan simulasi (membangun operator, memetakannya, dan mentranspilasi circuit hasilnya) tidak membutuhkannya sama sekali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fermionic simulation lives in a fixed particle-number sector {#fermionic-simulation-lives-in-a-fixed-particle-number-sector}"
msgstr "Simulasi fermionik berlangsung di sektor jumlah partikel tetap {#fermionic-simulation-lives-in-a-fixed-particle-number-sector}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both `_apply_unitary_` and `_linear_operator_` take an `nelec` argument and represent the state vector over the *fixed-particle-number determinant basis* for that `(norb, nelec)` sector, mirroring ffsim’s (and, transitively, PySCF’s) FCI space setup, rather than the full $2^{\\text{num\\_modes}}$-dimensional space a general qubit simulator would use. This is a much smaller space (its size is a product of binomial coefficients rather than a power of two), but it comes with a hard restriction. Only operators and gates that preserve particle number (and, in the spinful case, each spin species’ particle number individually) can be represented in it. An operator whose action would move amplitude to a different particle number has nowhere to put it.\n"
msgstr "Baik `_apply_unitary_` maupun `_linear_operator_` menerima argumen `nelec` dan merepresentasikan state vector di atas *basis determinan jumlah-partikel-tetap* untuk sektor `(norb, nelec)` itu, meniru setup ruang FCI milik ffsim (dan, secara transitif, PySCF), bukan ruang berdimensi $2^{\\text{num\\_modes}}$ penuh yang dipakai simulator qubit umum. Ruang ini jauh lebih kecil (ukurannya hasil kali koefisien binomial, bukan pangkat dua), tetapi datang dengan batasan keras. Hanya operator dan gate yang mempertahankan jumlah partikel (dan, pada kasus berspin, jumlah partikel tiap spesies spin secara terpisah) yang bisa direpresentasikan di dalamnya. Operator yang aksinya akan memindahkan amplitudo ke jumlah partikel berbeda tidak punya tempat untuk menaruhnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ffsim resolves this by rejecting such an operator outright: converting one to a linear operator raises a [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) naming which conservation law fails. That is the right default, because applying $\\exp(-i t H)$ for a Hamiltonian $H$ with a non-particle-conserving term would otherwise turn a would-be unitary into a non-unitary, physically-meaningless map.\n"
msgstr "ffsim menyelesaikannya dengan menolak operator semacam itu sama sekali: mengonversinya menjadi linear operator memunculkan [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) yang menyebutkan hukum kekekalan mana yang gagal. Itu default yang tepat, karena menerapkan $\\exp(-i t H)$ untuk Hamiltonian $H$ dengan suku yang tidak mempertahankan jumlah partikel akan mengubah sesuatu yang seharusnya uniter menjadi peta non-uniter yang tidak bermakna secara fisik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") surfaces that rejection from the operator it evolves.\n"
msgstr "[`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") meneruskan penolakan itu dari operator yang dievolusikannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") checks that its (embedded) rotation matrix is block-diagonal across the alpha/beta split in the spinful case, and raises a [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) if it mixes spin sectors.\n"
msgstr "[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") memeriksa bahwa matriks rotasinya (yang di-embed) berbentuk blok-diagonal di seluruh pembagian alpha/beta pada kasus spinful, dan memunculkan [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) kalau matriks itu mencampur sektor spin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Non-particle-preserving simulation is therefore out of reach in fermionic space, by construction of the fixed-sector representation, and that is the price of the compact FCI space which makes fermionic simulation tractable in the first place. If your algorithm needs particle-number-violating operators (for example, a qubit-native error channel, or an operator built for a mapped Hamiltonian that does not conserve particle numbers term by term), transpile to qubits first and simulate the resulting [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) with a qubit-level simulator instead. Any transpilation route works for this; the [fermionic circuit](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation) and [transpilation](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guides go into more detail, but [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") is a reasonable default choice.\n"
msgstr "Jadi, simulasi yang tidak menjaga jumlah partikel mustahil dilakukan di ruang fermionik, karena representasi sektor tetap memang dibuat begitu, dan itulah harga dari ruang FCI yang ringkas, yang sejak awal membuat simulasi fermionik jadi bisa dikerjakan. Kalau algoritmamu butuh operator yang melanggar jumlah partikel (misalnya error channel yang native ke qubit, atau operator yang dibuat untuk Hamiltonian hasil mapping yang tidak menjaga jumlah partikel suku demi suku), transpile dulu ke qubit lalu simulasikan [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) yang dihasilkan dengan simulator tingkat qubit. Rute transpilasi apa pun bisa dipakai untuk ini; panduan [fermionic circuit](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation) dan [transpilasi](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) membahasnya lebih detail, tapi [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") adalah pilihan default yang masuk akal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The block-spin convention for spinful systems {#the-block-spin-convention-for-spinful-systems}"
msgstr "Konvensi block-spin untuk sistem spinful {#the-block-spin-convention-for-spinful-systems}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`nelec` is typed `int | tuple[int, int]`, and its type, not a separate flag, is what selects one of the supported mode layouts:\n"
msgstr "`nelec` bertipe `int | tuple[int, int]`, dan tipenya, bukan flag terpisah, yang menentukan salah satu layout mode yang didukung:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An **int** selects the **spinless** interpretation. The `norb` modes are treated directly as spinless orbitals, and `nelec` is the total particle count.\n"
msgstr "Sebuah **int** memilih interpretasi **spinless**. `norb` mode diperlakukan langsung sebagai orbital spinless, dan `nelec` adalah jumlah total partikel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **pair** `(n_alpha, n_beta)` selects the **spinful** interpretation of `2 * norb` modes under a fixed **block-spin convention**. Modes `0 .. norb` are the alpha (spin-up) orbitals and modes `norb .. 2 * norb` are the beta (spin-down) orbitals. Each spin species is conserved *independently*; an alpha-only term can move an electron between alpha modes but never into a beta mode, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr "Sebuah **pasangan** `(n_alpha, n_beta)` memilih interpretasi **spinful** untuk `2 * norb` mode dengan **konvensi block-spin** yang tetap. Mode `0 .. norb` adalah orbital alpha (spin-up) dan mode `norb .. 2 * norb` adalah orbital beta (spin-down). Tiap spesies spin terjaga *secara independen*; suku khusus alpha bisa memindahkan elektron antar mode alpha tapi tidak pernah ke mode beta, dan sebaliknya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This dispatch happens at every ffsim-protocol entry point in this package (gate constructors, `_apply_unitary_placed_` implementations, and the native Rust kernel’s sector compilation), and it is the convention used throughout the [LUCJ](lucj#lucj-transpilation) and [SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) guides (for example, [`InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\") fills alpha occupations into modes `0 .. n_alpha` and beta occupations into modes `norb .. norb + n_beta`). It is worth contrasting this with the [`qiskit_fermions.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") module and [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") in general, which use *generic* mode indices with no inherent spin semantics (see the [fermionic circuit guide](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation)). The block-spin meaning is imposed only when a spinful `nelec` is supplied to a simulation call, not baked into the operator or circuit representation itself.\n"
msgstr "Dispatch ini terjadi di setiap entry point protokol ffsim di package ini (konstruktor gate, implementasi `_apply_unitary_placed_`, dan kompilasi sektor kernel Rust native), dan ini adalah konvensi yang dipakai di seluruh panduan [LUCJ](lucj#lucj-transpilation) dan [SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) (misalnya, [`InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\") mengisi okupasi alpha ke mode `0 .. n_alpha` dan okupasi beta ke mode `norb .. norb + n_beta`). Ini patut dibandingkan dengan modul [`qiskit_fermions.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") dan [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") secara umum, yang memakai indeks mode *generik* tanpa makna spin bawaan (lihat [panduan fermionic circuit](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation)). Makna block-spin baru diberlakukan saat `nelec` spinful diberikan ke pemanggilan simulasi, bukan tertanam di representasi operator atau circuit itu sendiri.\n"

